 # Cafe Big Mo's
 
-Next.js storefront for Cafe Big Mo's.
+Next.js storefront and WhatsApp ordering website for Cafe Big Mo's.
 
-## Development
+## Implemented
 
-```bash
-npm install
-npm run dev
-```
+### Part 0 — Foundation
+
+- Next.js App Router + TypeScript
+- Tailwind CSS
+- Framer Motion
+- Lucide React
+- Zustand
+- React Hook Form + Zod
+- ESLint + Prettier
+- project architecture and verification scripts
+
+### Part 1 — Brand system
 
-## Verification
+- Big Mo's colour and typography tokens
+- reusable UI primitives
+- transparent cafe logo
+- optimized Prayagraj and Haldwani outlet photography
+
+### Part 2 — Global layout
+
+- responsive sticky header
+- active desktop navigation
+- animated mobile navigation drawer
+- global footer
+- mobile order bar
+- breadcrumbs
+- reusable page hero
+- reusable CTA section
+- reusable outlet mini-card
+- placeholder routes for all global navigation targets
+- corrected Prayagraj and Haldwani map links
+
+## Commands
 
 ```bash
+npm run dev
 npm run lint
 npm run typecheck
 npm run build
-```
-
-Or run all checks:
-
-```bash
 npm run verify
 ```
 
-## Implementation status
-
-- Part 0: project foundation — complete
-- Part 1: assets + brand design system — complete
-- Part 2 onward: global layout, data, home, menu, cart, checkout and production pages
-
-## Part 1 assets
-
-Real supplied photography is organized by outlet:
-
-```text
-public/
-├── branding/logo.webp
-└── outlets/
-    ├── prayagraj/
-    └── haldwani/
-```
+## Part 2 visual verification
 
-Images are optimized to WebP for production use. The original supplied source images are not duplicated inside the repository.
+Run `npm run dev`, then check `/` plus `/menu`, `/about`, `/gallery`, `/outlets`, `/contact` and `/bag` at desktop and mobile widths. The header, mobile drawer, footer and fixed mobile ordering bar should remain consistent across routes.
